# Line endings are a repository decision, not a per-clone accident.
#
# This project's artifacts are compared and committed byte for byte: c_src/patches/gumbo-parser
# holds the patch series whose content the generator reproduces exactly, the .exs files beside them
# are read back as text, and the checksum file the precompiled archives are verified against is
# computed over those bytes. On a machine whose git converts line endings on checkout — GitHub's
# Windows runners do, and so does a default Windows install — every one of those files arrives as
# CRLF, the generator produces a patch that differs from the committed one by one byte per line, and
# the test suite fails somewhere far away from the cause. That is how this file came to be written:
# the Windows job found it.
#
# So: everything is LF, in the repository and in the working tree, on every platform. `text=auto`
# keeps git's own detection for files that are not text at all.
* text=auto eol=lf
